# Building at world scale, from a normal game start (docs/VISION.md §9): a
# holding put up on the real keys out of what is carried, somebody from the
# village put on the plot, eight world hours gone by, and the place found with a
# crop laid by and its thatch that much the worse for the weather.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/settlements.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --give=stone:6,deadwood:6,timber:4,reeds:6,scrap:6,pitch:2,rag:4,driftwood:4
# (--give is an armful of what the first four pieces cost: stone and dead wood
# for the hearth and the plot, timber and reeds for the store, plate and pitch
# for the catchment. Everything in it can be taken off the coast by hand; the
# taking is survival's proof, not this one's.)
coast calm
place spawn
wait 0.4
# Out of the village square to open ground, on the real keys. Near enough that
# somebody will walk over for the work; far enough to build.
walk -1,1 1.5
wait 0.5
shot 01-somewhere-to-put-it
# h opens the holding app: what can go up here, what it wants, and — in the
# stolen module's violet — what a machine would hear of the place.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
wait 0.6
shot 02-the-slate-asks-what-to-put-up with app:holding
# A hearth first, because that is the order a person builds in. It is the game's
# own fire: it lights the yard, and it can be slept beside and worked at.
choose build_hearth
tap use
await made 6
wait 0.5
shot 03-a-hearth-laid with app:holding
# A plot, a catchment to water it, and a store to put the crop in.
choose build_plot
tap use
await made 6
wait 0.4
choose build_catchment
tap use
await made 6
wait 0.4
choose build_store
tap use
await made 6
wait 0.5
shot 04-four-pieces-up with app:holding, holding
# Off the glass, and look at it.
tap pause
wait 0.8
shot 05-the-holding-at-noon with holding, piece:hearth, land:coast
# Somebody from the village takes the plot on: the row says "work it" before it
# is pressed, and the same body walks over and starts digging.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose piece_2
tap use
await staffed 4
tap pause
wait 1.4
shot 06-somebody-on-the-plot with staffed, holding_people
# Eight world hours. The holding is settled up from its own timestamp, not
# ticked: the plot is worked, the crop goes into the store, and everything
# standing is that much the worse for eight hours of weather.
hour 18
wait 1.6
await produced 6
shot 07-eight-hours-on with produced, stores, holding
await worn 4
shot 08-and-that-much-the-worse with worn, holding
# What it laid by, carried off the page and into the creel.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
wait 0.6
shot 09-what-a-machine-hears with app:holding
choose stores
tap use
await took 4
wait 0.5
shot 10-the-crop-in-the-creel with app:holding
tap pause
wait 0.6
# Dusk, which is when a holding is worth defending: the hearth is the one honest
# light in the landscape (docs/ART.md §10).
hour 20.5
wait 1.6
shot 11-the-holding-at-dusk with holding, piece:hearth
